supermodel: upload textures as RGBA8 instead of GL_FLOAT (legacy3d)

DecodeTexture decoded to GLfloat RGBA + uploaded GL_FLOAT (16 B/texel) while the
sheet storage is already GL_RGBA8. Decode straight to bytes (exact bit-replication)
and upload GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE: 4x less upload bandwidth, no driver conversion,
output-preserving (sources <=8-bit). Helps texture-churn (transitions).

